{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 118, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv on the direct input-to-output edge helps far more when that edge was empty (often reconnecting a disconnected cell) than when it replaces an existing op (exps 6-10 vs 1-5)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing the direct skip with a conv removes a useful residual path and was consistently negative across datasets (exps 1-5)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing edge 3 when edge 4 is absent leaves fewer routes to the output and can disconnect the cell, causing much larger drops (exps 21, 22, 29)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 5 absent, edge 3 is a primary path to the output, so deleting it is far more damaging (exps 21, 23, 29)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a skip on an empty direct edge restores connectivity and gradient flow, whereas replacing a conv with skip loses capacity (exps 81, 85 vs 86, 87, 90)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Turning an empty edge 5 into skip opens a route from node 2 to the output, while replacing a conv on edge 5 with skip discards capacity (exps 45, 50 vs 46, 47, 49)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Downgrading the edge-5 3x3 conv to an identity consistently hurt accuracy, especially on CIFAR-100 and ImageNet16 (exps 43, 47, 49)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Swapping a parameter-free pooling op on the last edge for a 3x3 conv adds substantial capacity and gave large gains (exps 11-18)."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a 3x3 conv on the node1-to-node2 edge with pooling removes learned features, unlike replacing none, skip, or 1x1 (exp 58 vs 55-57)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When the direct input-to-output edge is missing, adding a conv on node1-to-output adds a critical output path, giving larger gains (exps 91, 92 vs 93-100)."}], "tok": 31127, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "none"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "none"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "skip_connect"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "avg_pool_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "skip_connect", "none", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "none", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5,